2. PERMISSIONS — WHAT YOU MAY DO WITHOUT ASKING

   Subject to the conditions in Section 4, you are granted the following
   rights free of charge:

   a) VIEW — You may read and study the Software's source code.

   b) PERSONAL USE — You may run, modify, and use the Software for
      Personal Use as defined above.

   c) PRIVATE SHARING — You may share the Software or your modifications
      privately with individuals or within a small private group (e.g. a
      friend, colleague, or internal team), provided no public
      redistribution occurs. Using a shared copy remains subject to
      Sections 2(d) and 3(b).

   d) USE WITH THE NUKERHUGO AI SERVICE — You may run the Software,
      including your own private modifications of it, connected to the
      Nukerhugo AI Service, for your own work and for the internal work
      of your organization, whether or not that organization is
      commercial. Your use of the Nukerhugo AI Service remains subject
      to that service's own terms, plans, and limits. This permission
      does not allow public distribution of modified versions
      (Section 3a), selling, licensing, hosting, or otherwise offering
      the Software itself to others as a product or service, or using
      the Software commercially with services other than the Nukerhugo
      AI Service.

   e) YOUR OUTPUT — As between you and the Author, Your Output belongs
      to you. You may use it for any purpose, including commercially.
      Using Your Output is not Commercial Use of the Software. Terms of
      the AI model or service that generated it may also apply.

   f) CONTRIBUTING — You may create a Fork on a public code-hosting
      platform solely to prepare a contribution to the Author's
      official repository, provided that the Fork is not otherwise
      used, promoted, or distributed.

